2:[["$","div",null,{"className":"aeo-answer tl-dr","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Quick Answer:"}]," A CUET UG 2026 study plan should span 4-6 months and cover four sections: Section IA/IB (Languages), Section II (Domain Subjects), and Section III (General Test). CUET is NCERT-based, so mastering your Class 12 textbooks is 80% of the work. Study 4-6 hours daily, picking 1-2 domain subjects + 1 language + the General Test. Use an AI planner like PlanBot to rotate subjects daily, schedule NCERT revision cycles, and practice MCQs consistently."]}]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Why CUET Changed University Admissions in India"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["CUET (Common University Entrance Test) is the single entrance exam for admission to 250+ central, state, and private universities — including Delhi University, JNU, BHU, and BBAU. Over ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"14 lakh students"}]," appeared for CUET UG, making it one of the largest entrance exams in India."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Before CUET, Delhi University admissions were cutoff-based — meaning a single bad Class 12 board exam mark could shut you out of your dream college. CUET leveled the playing field: now, ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"your university admission depends on a standardized test, not your board percentage"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"That's a huge opportunity. It also means you need a strategy specifically built for CUET — not a generic board-exam approach."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Understanding the CUET UG Pattern"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"CUET is modular. You don't write the whole paper — you choose sections based on your target university and course."}],"\n",["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Section"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"What it Tests"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Subjects/Languages"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Questions to Attempt"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"IA"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Language (13 languages)"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"English, Hindi, Tamil, Bengali, etc."}],["$","td",null,{"children":"40 out of 50"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"IB"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Additional Languages (20)"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"French, German, Japanese, etc."}],["$","td",null,{"children":"40 out of 50"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"II"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Domain Subjects (27)"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Physics, Chemistry, History, Economics, etc."}],["$","td",null,{"children":"35-40 out of 45-50"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"III"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"General Test"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"GK, Reasoning, Quant, Current Affairs"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"50 out of 60"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Key rules:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["You can attempt a maximum of ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"6 subjects"}]," total across all sections"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Each section gets 45-60 minutes"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"+5 marks correct, -1 mark wrong"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Questions are ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"NCERT Class 12 level"}]," for domain subjects"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"The 5-Month CUET 2026 Master Plan"}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 1: NCERT Mastery (Months 1-2)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Complete and revise your Class 12 NCERT textbooks for chosen domain subjects"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 4-5 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The 80/20 Rule for CUET:"}]," 80% of CUET domain-subject questions come directly from NCERT. If you master NCERT, you'll score well. This is the most underused insight in CUET prep."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Split:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Domain Subject 1: 2 hours (NCERT reading + MCQ practice)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Domain Subject 2: 1.5 hours (if taking 2 domain subjects)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Language (English typically): 30 min reading + vocabulary"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"General Test basics: 30-45 min"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Key Actions:"}]}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Read each NCERT chapter ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"twice"}]," — once for understanding, once to make notes"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"After every chapter, solve 30-50 MCQs on that topic"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"For English, read 2-3 articles daily to build comprehension speed"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Start a Current Affairs habit (15-20 min daily news)"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How PlanBot Helps:"}]," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I'm preparing for CUET 2026 with Physics, Chemistry, and English. I can study 5 hours daily. Start with NCERT revision.\""}]," PlanBot builds a chapter-by-chapter schedule with built-in MCQ practice slots."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 2: MCQ Practice & Weak Areas (Months 3-4)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Convert NCERT knowledge into MCQ-solving speed and accuracy"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 5-6 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"What Changes:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Shift from reading to ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"solving"}]," (3:1 ratio of solving to reading)"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Start sectional mock tests"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Identify and target weak chapters"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Build General Test skills (Reasoning + Quant)"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Section-Wise Strategy:"}]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Domain Subjects (Physics/Chemistry/Bio/Math or Humanities subjects):"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Solve 50-80 MCQs daily across your subjects"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Maintain an \"error notebook\" — every wrong answer goes in with the correct concept"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Re-revise weak chapters every Sunday"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Language (English):"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"3-4 reading comprehension passages daily"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Vocabulary: 20 new words daily with usage"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"General Test:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Reasoning: 30 questions daily (series, coding-decoding, puzzles)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Quant: 20 questions daily (Class 10 level — simple but needs speed)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Current Affairs: Continue daily news + monthly magazine"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How PlanBot Helps:"}]," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I scored 55/100 in Physics sectional. Weak in Modern Physics and Optics.\""}]," PlanBot reallocates your week to focus on those chapters with targeted MCQ sets."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 3: Mocks & Revision (Month 5)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Full-length mocks, speed building, final revision"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 5-6 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"What Changes:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"4-5 full-length CUET mocks per week"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Deep analysis after each mock"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Daily revision of your error notebook"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"No new topics — consolidate only"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"The Mock-Day Routine:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Morning: Mock test (as per your actual exam timing)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Afternoon: Analysis — categorize every error (concept gap / silly mistake / time pressure)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Evening: Fix the biggest error category"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Subject Selection Strategy: The Hidden Lever"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"This is the most important decision in CUET prep"}]," — and most students get it wrong by copying what \"everyone takes.\""]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"The golden rules:"}]}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Check your target university's requirements."}]," Delhi University's B.Com requires specific subjects; JNU's BA programs have different needs. Map this ",["$","em",null,{"children":"before"}]," choosing."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Play to your strengths."}]," If you scored 95% in History and 75% in Math, take History as a domain subject."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Don't over-diversify."}]," Taking 5-6 subjects dilutes your focus. 2-3 well-prepared subjects beats 5 mediocre ones."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"English + General Test is a powerful combo."}]," Many universities accept this for humanities and management courses."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to Use PlanBot for CUET — A Practical Workflow"}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Choose your subjects first."}]," Decide your 1-2 domain subjects, language, and whether you're taking the General Test. Lock this in."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Tell PlanBot your setup:"}]," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I'm preparing for CUET 2026. Subjects: Physics, Chemistry, English, and General Test. Exam in 5 months. I can study 5 hours daily on weekdays, 7 on weekends.\""}]]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Follow the AI-generated plan."}]," PlanBot creates time-blocked daily schedules — say, 6-8am Physics NCERT, 5-7pm Chemistry MCQs, 9-9:30pm news. Each block has a clear goal."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Adjust dynamically."}]," Got a school exam? PlanBot compresses CUET prep without losing the schedule. ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"School exams this week, only 2 hours/day for CUET\""}]," → PlanBot prioritizes high-ROI tasks."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Use streaks for consistency."}]," CUET prep is a marathon. A 120-day streak is the difference between a DU central campus and a tier-3 college."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Common CUET Mistakes That Cost Seats"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Ignoring NCERT for \"advanced\" books"}]," — 80% of questions come from NCERT. Advanced books waste your time."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Taking too many subjects"}]," — dilutes focus and lowers each subject's score"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Not checking university subject requirements"}]," — taking subjects your target course doesn't accept"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Skipping the General Test"}]," — even humanities students benefit; it's a high-scoring section"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"No mock practice"}]," — CUET rewards MCQ-solving speed, not just knowledge"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Is CUET harder than boards?"}]," Not harder, but ",["$","em",null,{"children":"different"}],". Boards test descriptive answers; CUET tests fast MCQ-solving. You need MCQ practice even if your board scores are high."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Can I prepare for CUET alongside boards?"}]," Yes — that's the ideal approach since both are NCERT-based. About 70% of your board prep transfers to CUET directly."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How many CUET mocks should I solve?"}]," 25-35 full-length mocks in your cycle, with the bulk in the last 6 weeks. Analysis matters more than quantity."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Start Your CUET 2026 Prep Today"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"CUET rewards the prepared. With NCERT as your base and a structured daily plan, you can target top central universities — regardless of your past academic performance."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=cpm.planbot","children":"Get PlanBot free on Android"}]," and let the AI build your CUET 2026 study schedule."]}]]
